}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"18318841-c02c-43d1-a7bd-ccbba64f181d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Surface-like graphs", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"7fd4f12f-1af2-4be5-a057-83e8f755f59e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TessellationCurvature",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the combinatorial Gaussian curvature at a vertex of a regular \
or uniform map; its sign says spherical, flat or hyperbolic"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"b96aa9c5-2d84-4541-9d70-63633893007d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TessellationEulerCharacteristic",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the Euler characteristic V - E + F of a tessellation graph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"c14bb1d7-78fa-4df3-bf81-4cda315b1907"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TessellationGenus",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the orientable genus of a tessellation graph, from its Euler \
characteristic"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"fce7ca90-60b8-4443-a2e2-e73a23f2bf22"],

Cell["\<\
waits: a test whether a graph is surface-like at a scale, its metric balls \
discs and its metric shells cycles\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"01db0fb5-fb57-4a67-a78f-213a5a3c51ae"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Inflated substrates", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"aef84458-4df0-4106-ab60-c24b0582ccc4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["InflateGraph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] grows a fiber of extra vertices over every vertex, joined to \
its base vertex, with random edges between nearby fibers"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"a9cc9c83-1290-4443-adaf-3dac7247453f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["InflatedVertex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the i-th fiber vertex over a base vertex in a graph produced \
by InflateGraph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d07eaa07-cc73-40c4-a049-911666c2c6f9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Warped products", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"d416c2ef-98c3-41e1-9f22-0e282bb18c17"],

Cell["\<\
waits: the warped product of a base and a fiber as a graph; the Kasner graph \
in the dev repo's experimental code is one example\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d1ee21d8-7ace-4c71-a69d-23036aee3b30"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

